hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"472","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Allah has pardoned my Ummah for what occurs in their hearts, as long as they do not act upon it or speak about it."
"473","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When a slave obeys his Lord and his master, he will have two rewards."" The narrator stated: When Abu Rafi' was freed, he began to weep. He was asked: Why are you weeping? He replied: I used to have two rewards, and now one of those rewards is gone."
"474","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the servant (slave) of any one of you brings his food to him, and if he does not seat him with himself, then he should give him one or two morsels, because he has endured hardship and heat in preparing it."
"475","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""When the servant of any one of you brings food, let him make him sit with him and give him a morsel, for he has endured the hardship of cooking and the heat of the fire as well."
"476","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever frees his share in a jointly owned slave, it is obligatory upon him that if he has wealth, he should grant the slave complete freedom from his own wealth. And if he does not have wealth, then the value of the slave should be assessed justly, then regarding the share which has not been freed, the slave should be told to strive to earn and obtain his freedom himself, but no hardship should be imposed upon him."
"477","Urwah narrated from this chain the same narration, and said: Regarding the share of the partner who did not free him: The slave will be told to earn and obtain his freedom himself. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""If he has wealth, he will be freed from his wealth; if he does not have wealth, the slave will earn and obtain freedom."
"478","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding the man who finds his wealth with a destitute person in exactly the same condition; he is more entitled to it than anyone else. And 'Umra is permissible. And when a slave is jointly owned by two men, and one of them frees his share for his partner (co-owner)."
"479","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever frees his share in a jointly owned slave, and if he has wealth and there is no partner with him, then freeing him from his wealth becomes obligatory upon him."
"480","With the same (previous) chain of narration, it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""When a slave dies in such a state that he worships his Lord well and is also sincere towards his master, then Allah frees him (from Hell)."
"481","Syedna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: Barirah’s husband was an Abyssinian slave, his name was Mughith. It is as if I am seeing him circling behind her (Barirah, may Allah be pleased with her) in the streets of Madinah."
"482","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said regarding (his beloved son) Ibrahim’s (may Allah be pleased with him) mother (Maria al-Qibtiyya, may Allah be pleased with her) at the time when she gave birth to him: “Her son has set her free.”"
"483","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Any slave woman who gives birth to a child from her master, she will be free after his (the master's) death."
